<title>LEBANON: All Lebanese t-bill yields fall.</title>
<headline>All Lebanese t-bill yields fall.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>All yields fell on Lebanese treasury bills, according to weekly rates issued by the Bank of Lebanon on Monday.</p>
<p>It announced the following interest rates for its February 6 issues (previous week in brackets):</p>
<p>    Term		     Discount		     Yield</p>
<p>				(percent)		   (percent)</p>
<p>    Three months	  13.49 (13.60)	     13.96 (14.08)</p>
<p>    Six months	    13.94 (14.44)	     14.98 (15.56)</p>
<p>    12 months	     13.33 (13.68)	     15.37 (15.84)</p>
<p>    24 months   (Interest payable twice yearly) 16.34 (17.14)</p>
<p>-Beirut editorial (961 1) 602057 745307  745308</p>
</text>
